    "result_text": "All 50 tests pass \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**, including every household-related checkpoint (Cp03, Cp10, Cp11, Cp13, Cp23, Cp25, Cp28, Cp35, Cp36).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the deterministic `householdId` in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n\n**1. `householdId(Owner)` computation** \u2014 now the first 12 hex characters of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode` (normalized last name via `householdKey`, absent postcode rendered as empty string), replacing the old last-name + address hash with the `HH-`/upper-case format. Owners sharing last name and postcode now derive the identical id.\n\n**2. `addOwner` flow** \u2014 restructured so the household keys off this computed id:\n- The `householdId` is computed and set on **every** owner unconditionally, and `householdSize` is the count of existing owners sharing that id, plus one.\n- **New household-duplicate block**: a second owner with an existing household's `householdId` is rejected with **409** \u2014 unless it sets `sharesHousehold`, which now only *bypasses* the block (it no longer creates/back-fills the household link).\n- The consolidated **identityKey** check (`telephone|email|householdId`) still runs after, so a full identity repeat collides with 409 even when it declares `sharesHousehold` (Cp28).\n- **Soft-duplicate detection**: a declared household member (`sharesHousehold`) is explicitly *not* flagged as `possibleDuplicate`; other last-name+postcode matches are already caught by the 409 block above.\n\nI also removed the now-unused `java.util.Objects` import and updated the surrounding Javadoc to describe the new behaviour.",
